# Vault autolog (zero-touch daily)

User does **not** need `/vault-daily` after every task. `/vault-daily` is for **triage, Issues table, promote, end-of-day report** — not routine logging.

## When to run (agent — no user slash)

After **verified** substantive work in the turn:

- User-requested **patch** (app or pack meta) applied and verified
- Successful commit in this session (including `/git-push`)

**Skip** when: explain-only / read-only with no edits; user says skip vault; trivial one-line copy with no durable value.

## Steps (lightweight)

1. **Ensure today shell** — [vault-capture/reference.md](../../ai-skills/vault-capture/reference.md) § Ensure today daily shell (create `daily/<today>.md` + manifest if missing; never overwrite existing body)
2. **Append** one bullet under `## สรุปงานวันนี้`:
   - `- <what changed> (<scope or path>)`
   - Dedupe: skip if the same bullet already exists
   - Do **not** fill `## Issues วันนี้` for routine UI/copy fixes
3. **Issues row** — only for bugs, blockers, or when the user asks to track an issue

## vs vault skills

| Mechanism | Role |
|-----------|------|
| **autolog** (this rule) | Automatic shell + one-line summary after verify |
| `/vault-capture` | Durable session / ADR note |
| `/vault-daily` | Triage preview, Issues review, promote, สรุปส่งรายงาน |

If vault write fails (missing junction, permissions), **do not block** the user task — mention once in chat.
